  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting Social and Economic Resilience of Vulnerable Women and Girls (SECuRE) II 2021-2024</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">From 2018 until 2021, with funding from Sida, the IRC began implementing an integrated programme with the goal; to increase the safety of women and promote their economic and social resilience in vulnerable areas of Jordan and Lebanon. The IRC will continue working toward this goal, with interventions centred on the following three refined programme objectives.  These build upon the success and outcomes realised through three years of SECuRE implementation, and sets out further ambitions regarding the integration of activities and the sustainability of interventions:
Goal:  Women and girls are safer and are economically and socially resilient.
Objectives:
1.Women safely generate income and assets and are able to safely use and control resources
2.Women and girls are empowered and supported to shape and contribute to their communities and homes 
3.Women and girls are protected and supported to recover from the consequences of Gender-Based Violence (GBV)</narrative>
  </description>
